---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Accessibility | CBO Salud"
  description="Accessibility statement for the CBO Salud website: our commitment, measures taken, conformance status and how to contact us."
>
  <section class="bg-brand-50 py-16 border-b border-brand-100">
    <div class="container-main max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Accessibility</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4">
        Accessibility Statement
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-500">Last updated: October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div
      class="container-main max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray prose-headings:font-bold prose-headings:text-gray-900 prose-p:text-gray-600 prose-p:leading-relaxed max-w-none"
    >
      <h2>1. Our commitment</h2>
      <p>
        We want anyone to be able to read the information on this website, regardless of ability or
        the technology they use. We work to make the content understandable and operable with a
        screen reader, with a keyboard, with page zoom or with high-contrast settings.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Conformance status</h2>
      <p>
        This website is partially conformant with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)
        2.2, level AA. Most content meets the criteria, and we continue to review and fix those it
        does not yet meet. We do not hold external certification of conformance.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Measures taken</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Semantic structure with hierarchical headings, navigation regions and real lists.</li>
        <li>
          Alternative text on informative images; decorative images are hidden from assistive
          technology.
        </li>
        <li>
          A “Skip to content” link as the first element of each page, so keyboard users do not have
          to tab through the menu.
        </li>
        <li>Visible focus indicator on links, buttons and controls.</li>
        <li>Colour contrast reviewed for both text and interactive elements.</li>
        <li>The system's reduced-motion preference is respected.</li>
        <li>
          Responsive layout that keeps content readable when the page is zoomed or viewed on small
          screens.
        </li>
        <li>
          Each page declares its language in the markup, so screen readers pronounce it correctly.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Known limitations</h2>
      <p>
        This site embeds no third-party content. Links to Google Maps, Instagram or the
        physiotherapy booking platform open external sites, whose accessibility is outside our
        control.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Feedback and contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you find an accessibility barrier, email us at <a
          href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}
          class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{SITE.email}</a
        > or call <a href={SITE.phoneTel} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700"
          >{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a
        >. Tell us the page and the specific problem. We will reply as soon as possible and, if the
        content is not accessible to you, we will provide it another way.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Review</h2>
      <p>This statement is reviewed periodically, alongside the rest of the site's content.</p>

      <p>
        See also our <a href="/en/legal-notice" class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700"
          >Legal Notice</a
        >
        and our <a href="/en/privacy-policy" class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700"
          >Privacy Policy</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
